& [PreservedIntent]
  + Cantor should serve an inference host with the SOP terms clauses records relationships and proof relevant to a request
  + the lightest useful inference operation should unfold more SOP only when subject criteria require it
  + signed compiled material must retain stable semantic identity and changed material must be recompiled
  + after the full native lifecycle became directly callable through MCP the next leverage point is to stop resending its complete body on every call

& [Problem]
  + a NativeLifecycleValidationRequest intentionally owns its complete causal lineage and may approach eight megabytes
  + Slice8 is stateless so every validation call must transport that whole request
  + a bare hash cannot reconstruct omitted meaning and must not become authentication authorization or semantic evidence by itself

& [RequestedSlice]
  + define an immutable content-addressed custody registry whose entries retain complete normalized lifecycle requests
  + compile a compact handle from the exact retained request and bind protocol request identity operation and request digest
  + register by returning a new registry value rather than mutating hidden global state
  + resolve only by exact handle equality and complete registry replay then return the retained request for ordinary Slice7 validation
  + make equal registration explicit rather than silently overwriting or aliasing an entry

& [IdentityAndBounds]
  + registry entry and handle profiles must be exact and all JSON forms must reject unknown fields
  + keys digests entry counts roots and non-authority statements must be derivable from retained values
  + registry entry count and aggregate retained-byte ceilings must be finite and checked before successor publication
  + returned handles must be materially smaller than their retained request in the measured fixture

& [Honesty]
  + lookup means exact retained bytes were found and replayed not that meaning was recreated from a digest
  + custody coherence is not lifecycle validity truth correctness safety permission freshness persistence authentication signing admission installation deployment execution or effect authority
  + refused lifecycle requests may be retained for exact diagnosis but custody must never reclassify their core validation outcome

& [Security]
  + handle substitution request substitution root tampering count tampering cross-registry lookup unknown fields and resource excess must fail closed
  + no secret filesystem process provider network clock environment dynamic loading or remote host enters the pure P0 form
  + a later mutable or persistent MCP registry requires its own specification for concurrency lifetime eviction authorization and recovery

& [Acceptance]
  + equal inputs produce byte-identical handle entry registry and resolved request
  + resolved request validation equals direct Slice7 validation for valid and refused cases
  + registration and resolution preserve all Slice8 non-authority
  + focused debug optimized release warnings-denied lint format evidence and diff gates pass before closure

& [ExplicitNonGoals]
  + MCP state host installation persistence database expiry eviction global uniqueness authentication authorization build runner signing admission installation deployment execution internal llama.cpp FPGA remote OneDrive EVO-X2 and Minecraft
